     "page": 1,
     "text": "SUMMARY - Garrison Inc Medical Group\nPatient: Christopher Gutierrez DOB: 05/27/1986 Sex: M MRN: 787837\n\nEncounters:\n 2024-12-27 annual physical BP 116/83 Wt 121\n 2024-07-27 back strain BP 123/91 Wt 129\n 2024-02-24 flu shot BP 127/89 Wt 124\n 2023-09-23 Pulmonary embolism / DVT BP 116/86 Wt 128\n 2023-04-22 flu shot BP 121/83 Wt 130\n 2022-11-19 URI BP 131/84 Wt 125\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • Pulmonary embolism / DVT (0.4 yrs ago; recurrent; provoked) - controlled; meds: rivaroxaban 20 mg\n\n**Detailed Clinical Summary:**\n\nOn December 27, 2024, Mr. Christopher Gutierrez, a 38-year-old male, visited for his physical. During this visit, his blood pressure was measured at 116/83 mmHg and his weight was recorded at 121 pounds. Physical examination findings were within normal limits. He reported no significant symptoms apart from mild back discomfort unrelated to his primary \n\nOn July 27, 2024, Mr. Gutierrez presented with complaints of back strain. His blood pressure was noted 123/91 mmHg and his weight at 129 pounds. Upon examination, his back showed mild tenderness, but no signs of significant pathology were found. This incident was managed conservatively with recommendations for rest and over-the-counter analgesics.\n\nDuring his visit on February 24, 2024, for a flu shot, Mr. Gutierrez's blood pressure was 127/89 mmHg and his weight 124 pounds. He reported no acute issues, and his physical examination was otherwise unremarkable. He received annual influenza vaccination without complications.\n\nOn September 23, 2023, Mr. Gutierrez was admitted with a diagnosis of pulmonary embolism and deep vein thrombosis (DVT). His blood pressure at that time was 116/86 mmHg, and his weight was 128 pounds. Detailed workup confirmed the diagnosis of DVT, and he was started on anticoagulation therapy with rivaroxaban 20 mg daily. After an extensive evaluation, the event was deemed provoked. He has been compliant with his medication regimen and has not experienced any recurrent episodes, indicating that his condition is well controlled.\n\nDuring a visit on April 22, 2023, for a flu shot, his blood pressure was 121/83 mmHg and his weight 130 pounds. He reported no new complaints, and a general physical exam revealed no abnormalities. He received his flu vaccine uneventfully.\n\nOn November 19, 2022, Mr. Gutierrez presented with symptoms of an upper respiratory infection (URI). His blood pressure was recorded at 131/84 mmHg and his weight at 125 pounds. He was managed symptomatically with appropriate recommendations for hydratio"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "n and rest. There were no complications related to this encounter.\n\n**Social History:**\nMr. Gutierrez has a history of tobacco use, having smoked cigarettes at a rate of one per day starting from June 21, 2005. He successfully quit smoking on May 12, 2022, and has been tobacco-free for approximately 2.2 years. His disclosure regarding his tobacco use was honest and consistent.\n\n**Family History:**\nMr. Gutierrez's mother had a history of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), which she developed at the age of 70. Unfortunately, she passed away prior to the period, so her current age at death is unknown. \n\nThe above summary provides a comprehensive overview of Mr. Gutierrez's medical history, including his current controlled condition of pulmonary embolism/DVT, recent relevant visits, and social and family history factors. His adherence to his prescribed anticoagulation therapy with rivaroxaban has been exemplary, and there have been no recurrences of his condition.\n"
